WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.960
Shizukesa to yasuragi ga...
<i>Silence and peace...</i>

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.170
...tooku de maneku kara.
<i>... beckon from afar.</i>

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.250
Mou sukoshi saki ni made...
<i>So, I feel I can go...</i>

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.610
...yukisouna kiga suru.
<i>... just a little further ahead.</i>

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.550
Tada te wo toriatte...
<i>We only take each other's hand...</i>

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.920
kooritsuku yoru wo...
<i>not to fall victim to the...</i>

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.890
...koete.
<i>... freezing night.</i>

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.360
Kizutsuite utsumuita...
<i>I was hurt and downcast...</i>

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.460
...tokini deatta kara...
<i>... at the time we met.</i>

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:42.500
Setsunasa ga nakunareba...
<i>If my heartache were to disappear...</i>

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.670
...hanarete yuku youde.
<i>... I feel that you would leave me.</i>

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.840
Yogoreta mizu no ue...
<i>Because it's reflected on tainted water...</i>

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.010
dakara tsuki no kage ga...
<i>the silhouette of the moon...</i>

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.140
...kirei de.
<i>... looks beautiful.</i>

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.650
Sore wa kanashimi no...
<i>That is a tale...</i>

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.820
...kataru monogatari.
<i>... telling of sorrow.</i>

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.360
Koi to yobu koto ni...
<i>I am still hesitant...</i>

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.990
...mada tameratte iru.
<i>... to call it 'love. '</i>

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.070
Itetsuita yoru ni...
I wonder if the closest stars...

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.670
chikakunaru hoshi wa...
<i>on a frozen night...</i>

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.340
kimi ga iru yume wo...
<i>will always be kind...</i>

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:28.300
...itsumade misete kureru darou?
<i>... and give me dreams of you?</i>

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.940
Why Takayama of all places?

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.840
My parents said they can work anywhere
as long as there's Internet access.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.720
SOHO?
(Small Office Home Office)

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.750
The so-called literary profession.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:10.720
I mean, yeah, I think the depth of
culture here is definitely amazing.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.730
It's a treasure mine of folklore, but...

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.000
But?

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:28.470
I guess sometimes it doesn't sit well
when a place feels too much..."inside."

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.340
Inside? What do you mean?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.750
Why are we meeting in Hida anyway?

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.380
Because, well... I'm in Takayama,
so I wanted to have a look around.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.690
Still, it sure is cold.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:48.430
What'd you expect?
It's cold in winter. Besides...

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.490
Huh?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.530
Oh, this?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.390
Helba!

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.020
What do we have here?

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:29.030
"I would like to discuss some matters
concerning recent incidents in 'The World.'"

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.440
"I apologize in advance, but if you
are interested, please meet me at...

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.480
...'The Place Where the
Carpenter's Daughter Sleeps' - Helba."

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.040
Helba? Is that a character
in the Epitaph?

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.090
Helba, Queen of the Dark.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.880
That's not what I heard.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.520
What did you hear?

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.290
That she's a great legendary hacker.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.920
That's interesting, but I don't like it.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.170
Hey, can you give me some details?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.170
In the Epitaph, Helba is
a well-informed strategist.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:13.280
She's much sharper than
Apeiron, King of the Light.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.880
That's why it's intriguing
that a hacker is using her name.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.580
And what don't you like?

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.180
The timely manner of the mail.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.660
It means that Helba
knew about our meeting.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.800
It could be coincidence...

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.670
...but it's also possible that
our E-mail has been hacked.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.230
There's one other thing.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:41.470
They say strange things always happen...

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.140
...if you delve deeply into
the "Epitaph ofTwilight."

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.280
It's supposed to unfold just like
the 100th tale in 'The 100 Stories.'

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.610
Or so they say.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.810
Mr. Tokuoka from Tokyo.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.960
Mr. Tokuoka. You have a phone call.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:01.150
If you are here, please
come to the front desk.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.960
Did you tell somebody you'd be here?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.500
No.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.640
This is kind of eerie.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.130
What's wrong?

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:38.000
The bastard had the nerve
to ask how determined I was.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.620
It was a man?

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.000
He said he represents Helba.
Bith the Black.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.340
Is that a character from the Epitaph as well?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.640
He's Helba's trusted retainer.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.010
That means their surveillance
isn't limited to inside the net.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.550
Yeah.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.020
I don't like this. I really don't like this!

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.060
That's why I'm going to check it out.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.630
This is " The Place Where the
Carpenter's Daughter Sleeps"?

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.670
It's told that when this
three-storied pagoda was built...

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:21.700
...the palace carpenter's daughter was
killed by her parents and buried here.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.840
Well, that's rather...

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.380
Nobody here fits his profile.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.750
Yeah.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.400
Hi. What's up?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:42.990
Barking
Hot-Blooded
500 Lohan

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.400
Um, I don't understand
the meaning of your E-mail.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:48.090
<i>E- mail?</i>

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:54.170
'Sadako' is a character in the movie "The Ring."
In the US version, she is 'Samara.'
What does " Please come to the place
closely related to Sadako" mean?

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.270
<i>Hold on a second!
When did you get that E-mail?</i>

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.810
Just a minute ago.

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.310
Okay. I'll call you again later.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:11.120
This may be a bit of a problem.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.460
Do you think it's a threat?

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:14.960
Unusual
Ghostly
Remnant

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.450
Do you think it's a threat?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.740
It's probably to
demonstrate that Mai...

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.210
...and possibly even Yukichin
are both under surveillance.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.140
Okay, I see... All right.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:38.140
Isn't it possible someone from CC Corp.
is just using the name Helba?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.080
I doubt it.

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:44.350
They don't want us
sniffing around too much, right?

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:47.830
But they'd threaten us more directly.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.300
They wouldn't use such
a roundabout method.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.760
True.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:57.130
Anyway, is there a reason we need
to go from one place to another?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.130
To find that out...

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:04.740
...let's stick around with Helba or Bith
the Black or whatever a little longer.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.880
So, where is this place
that's related to Sadako?

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:12.120
About that... I don't know any Sadako.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.450
The only Sadako I know is
a character in a horror movie.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.020
But that couldn't be it, right?

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.390
A horror movie?

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.790
She's a kind of psychic.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.420
I see. Then it must be there.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.970
Huh? Y- You know where it is just from that?

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.410
Tomokichi Fukurai.
Professor Fukurai Memorial Museum

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:45.150
He used to be a professor
at Tokyo Imperial University.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.690
He was so into clairvoyance
and spirit photography research...

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.850
...that he was ordered to
take a leave of absence...

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.290
...because it was inappropriate to conduct
research of that nature at the university.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.230
He's originally from Takayama.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.760
Wow.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.000
Is that so?

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.800
Hida is a mysterious place, huh?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.870
It's in a horribly inconvenient
mountain location...

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.840
...but I hear people have been living here
since theJomon era (c. 400 B.C.).

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:12.850
A grade school kid
told me about the story of...

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:16.940
..." The Okame Stone beneath
the streetlight of Ebizaka."

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.210
What is it about?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.840
That's all there is to it.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.290
Hey...

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.550
No, no, no. What do you mean
that's all there is to it?

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.220
Actually, that's all there is.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:32.560
But after a long time, even
a story like that could become legend.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:36.800
What I'm referring to
is the power of the land.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:40.840
When Dr. Fukurai was born here,
he might have tried to look at the world...

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.400
...in a different paradigm
from other people.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.480
Are you saying there's a connection
between that and the "Epitaph ofTwilight"?

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:54.890
A paradigm shift? I see.
I never thought of it that way.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:02.900
What is the "Epitaph ofTwilight"
about anyway?

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:10.630
Sprites without shadows are being eaten away
by a woe known as the "Cursed Wave,"

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.270
...and are on the verge of extinction.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.680
It is a wave, so it just steadily
advances closer and closer...

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:22.270
...and there is no way to fight it.
In the midst of their despair...

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.910
...Apeiron, King of the Light,
and Helba, Queen of the Dark...

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:31.520
...finally decide to form an alliance
to face the crisis together.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.160
But they have no way to fight it, right?

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:39.870
There's a legend. It says,
"When the Wave emerges...

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:46.170
...three beings with shadows will set forth
in search of the Twilight Dragon."

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:51.370
So, the dragon can fight the wave.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:55.470
A human and two half-sprites with shadows...

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.350
...set out on a journey to the
Wavering Peninsula at the edge of the world.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:06.080
Assisting them halfway in their journey
is Fili the White and Bith the Black.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.330
So, that's Bith.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:21.340
I wonder what he wants us to do here?

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:29.380
Hey, mister. Are you Mr. Tokuoka?

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:34.660
I don't think I'm mistaken.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:38.620
Who are you?

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.660
That doesn't matter.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:44.490
If you are Mr. Tokuoka, I've
been asked to give you this.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.400
Dual-Sided Demon?

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.130
Victory Wish?

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:56.370
Lady, where'd you get this?

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.410
Fearful, so fearful.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.910
Lady, who asked you to give me this?

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.470
- Hey!
- Fearful, so fearful.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.420
She says she's scared.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.960
What's that mean?

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:19.930
Hey...

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.030
Hey, wait! Hey!

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.560
The Dual-Sided Demon is at
Senko Temple, but Victory Wish?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:48.960
I don't even know what
that Dual-Sided thing means.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.960
It refers to a powerful man in Hida...

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:55.060
...from the mythical age, who had
two heads, four arms, and four legs.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.440
The embodiment of good
and evil coexisting in one body.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.200
Jekyll and Hyde with no on/off switch.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.040
Is there really a meaning to all this?

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.410
Meaning to what?

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:11.110
Takayama sightseeing,
following clues given to us.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:14.420
Like I said before, I don't know.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:19.120
But what we are doing is proceeding
to new locations by solving small puzzles.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.060
Then we find a clue that
points us to the next location.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:25.960
Doesn't this activity
remind you of something?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.760
An RPG...

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.300
The truth of the matter is,
we don't know the rules...

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.810
...or what kind of last
boss is waiting for us.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:37.640
But, well, if that's how the other side
wants to play, I'll go as far as I need to.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:41.610
Maybe we should just enjoy it.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:43.740
Well, if that's the way it is...

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.580
...we have no choice. We'll have
to rely on the strategy guide.

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:47.810
Huh?

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:52.290
My mom is editor of the local magazine.
She knows a lot about that sort of thing.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.790
That would be the
Sakurayama Hachiman Temple.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:00.420
That's where it originated. Yes...
Lord Takefurukuma...

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:05.460
...who came to exorcize the Dual-Sided
Demon, built it for his victory wish.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.010
Shall I send you some documents?

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:10.770
Oh, okay. By the way, Kyoko...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.540
I got a call from Mr. Hokiguchi
in Koufu a moment ago.

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:15.780
He said he saw you walking
with a middle-aged man.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.580
<i>Who are you with?</i>

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.520
I'm showing around a guest from Tokyo.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:24.220
- <i>Is he middle-aged?</i>
- Is that what bothers you?

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.190
<i>What?</i>

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.730
It's Dad.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:34.890
I'm on my way home from
a meeting. Want a ride?

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.400
You came all the way from Tokyo
about the "Epitaph ofTwilight"?

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:48.550
That's odd. You're
the second one today.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.210
Was there someone else here?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.910
Yeah, the person I just had a meeting with.
He asked me if I would consider translating it.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.510
You're kidding. Did you accept?!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:01.190
No. I don't want to get involved with that.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:04.230
Do you mean because it's the
100th tale ofThe 100 Stories?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.930
Not just that. There is
a problem with the original text.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:12.770
Oh, yeah. You don't know how
that work came out into the public.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:15.270
Huh?

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:20.140
It first appeared on author
Emma Wielant's personal website.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:25.350
However, it was available on-line
for only a very short amount of time.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:30.580
By the time some fantasy researchers
and occultists noticed the work,

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:35.250
the original was already lost by her death.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:40.560
She died at the age of 28. The cause
of death was a traffic accident.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:43.600
However, about <i>70%</i> of the text...

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.610
...has been restored by several
passionate followers. But then...

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.870
"The World" was released.

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:54.880
Word got out that the prototype
of"The World" called "Fragment"...

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:59.890
...was designed by genius programmer
Harald Hoerwick using her work as a model.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.920
It completely changed the situation.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.890
Oh, I get it!

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.950
Do you understand?

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.930
Fakes and alterations, right?

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.630
Since it was first introduced as text data...

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.640
...anyone could easily
copy and alter the content.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:21.270
So her work was butchered and the quality
of it after "The World" is unbearable to see.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.240
Even if the missing portions
of the text were to be found...

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:28.270
...it would be very difficult to discern
whether it is the original or not.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:32.270
As a result, the full scope
of the story is still unknown.

00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:37.660
That is the "Epitaph ofTwilight."

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:44.660
Uh... Can you tell me about the person
who asked about the translation?

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.100
If you don't mind, that is.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:51.700
He was a smart dresser, but there was
a kind of gloomy atmosphere about him.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.370
Do you have his business card?

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.750
That's a pretty fake name.

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.190
Thanks.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:12.190
Thank you.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.690
Do you think Bith and Ichiro Sato
are the same person?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.290
Maybe. Well, since we're here...

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.860
...let's take a look around before
heading to the next place.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.010
Were Emma and Harald acquaintances?

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:29.070
To Emma, yes. But to
Harald, she was more.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:31.710
Unrequited love?

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:37.680
Probably, yes. I don't
know much about Harald...

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:41.690
...but I have a feeling Emma
loved his talent, not him.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:45.380
When they first met, Emma had
a lover who was 20 years older than her.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.930
What?!

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.990
Apparently, she was very beautiful...

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:52.330
...but she was also
very high-maintenance.

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.390
A rich girl?

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.330
Her family ran an old winery.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:59.770
Really... So, how the hell did she meet Harald?

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.770
It turns out she wasn't
just a girl from a rich family.

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:06.370
She lost her mother at an early age.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:10.040
Her father also died when she was 18.

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:13.380
By his will, her uncle
was made her guardian...

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:17.750
...but this man proposed adopting
her to get her inheritance.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.120
What a crook.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.860
But Emma was smart.

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:22.990
She refused?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:27.830
Yeah. But she couldn't accept
the inheritance until she turned 20.

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:32.600
So, she entered nursing
school to support herself.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.430
Yeah. Good going, Emma.
I could fall in love with her, too.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:43.380
However, on the morning
of her 20th birthday...

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:46.720
...overwork and stress finally caught up
with her, and Emma coughed up blood.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.290
Hemoptysis...

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:53.790
Luckily, it didn't get out of control,
and she quickly returned to health...

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.300
...but on the advice from her physician,
Emma stayed at a health resort...

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.300
...in Southern France for
a period of time. That was where...

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:04.330
...she had an otherworldly experience
that would influence her life from then on.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:10.370
Because of this experience,
she studied Rudolf Steiner's...

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.150
...Anthroposophy.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.700
That's right. It's all come together, hasn't it?

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:20.050
If I remember correctly, Harald
sought for the relationship between...

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:24.780
...humans and computers and pursued
anthroposophy as a starting point.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.920
In the same way, Emma was
submerged in that idea...

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.090
...in an effort to understand
the existence of the world.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.070
Then she wrote the
"Epitaph ofTwilight"...

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:37.670
And Harald designed "Fragment."

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.430
I still don't get it, though.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:44.100
Yeah. Something is still missing...

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.840
...to explain the things
happening in "The World."

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:49.440
You've got nothing left?

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:53.350
What's left is... It's not clear
how much of it is true...

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.390
...but they say there
was more to the story.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.920
I'm all ears.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:02.850
When Emma had the accident,
she was on her way to meet Harald.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:07.530
He waited and waited for Emma under
a large gingko tree on top of a hill...

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.730
...not knowing of her death.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:21.850
<i>Yes?</i>

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.880
Kyo? What's this about?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:26.040
<i>E- mail?</i>

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.850
E-mail. It doesn't make any sense.

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.950
<i>Sorry. That's something
I had someone forward to you.</i>

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:35.520
Would you be a dear and read it to me?

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.260
<i>You're being weird. Okay, I'll read it.</i>

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:43.870
<i>"The cross of smoke rises.
Lake of water sprites. "</i>

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.030
<i>I think that was it.</i>

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:47.570
Got it.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:51.240
<i>Hey, hey, is Mr. Tokuoka with you?
He may not look it...</i>

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:54.870
<i>... but he's pretty rich.
Make him buy you dinner!</i>

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.280
I'll consider it. Well, talk to you later.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.920
Let's go to the next one.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:04.580
We have to go back
down these, don't we?

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.970
This place caught fire several times...

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:22.940
...but on one occasion, the rising smoke
formed the shape of a cross.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:24.480
Even though it's a temple?

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.840
That's why it's become a local legend.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:31.080
Looks like this is the final confrontation.

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:38.760
Past here, there's a lake
where water sprites appear.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.790
This is very well thought-out.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.010
Pleased to meet you.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.050
Bith the Black?!

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:01.580
Ichiro Sato!

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:05.310
Oh, you already know my other
name. That makes things quicker.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:08.440
In what way? It's a
fake name, isn't it?

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:09.890
What's wrong with that?

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:11.250
You're really getting on my nerves.

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:14.630
Names are just symbols.

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:15.130
Ringing Ears

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:15.560
Noisy

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:16.060
Like Kyo and Kyoko Tohno...

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:16.560
Sacred

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.530
Like Kyo and Kyoko Tohno...

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:22.630
...and Sieg and Tomonari Kasumi.

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:26.300
Though they are different,
they all stand for the same thing.

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:31.240
All right, then I have a question.
What are <i>you</i> actually, then?

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:35.710
I am a representative.
I said so in the beginning.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:39.080
Queen Helba has many clients.

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:40.980
Hackers have clients?

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:45.580
Now, now, that isn't
like you, Mr. Tokuoka.

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:50.650
Hackers also make excellent
security analysts. Do they not?

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:58.670
Why don't we sit down and talk?
How about some food?

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:06.210
I may just be the only one... but there's
gotta be something much better in this town...

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.250
...like Hida beef or Hoba miso.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.270
And of all places, why here?

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:16.080
If that's what you prefer, then
please have that together later.

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:17.780
I'm fine here.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:19.020
Isn't this a tad skimpy?

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:21.290
We can talk about that later.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:27.400
Harald designed "Fragment"
based on the "Epitaph ofTwilight."

00:23:27.470 --> 00:23:32.030
To be more precise, if he had merely
used its worldview as a model...

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:35.170
...the current chaos in "The World"
wouldn't have happened. Right?

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:38.940
Agreed. Then why is it happening?

00:23:40.010 --> 00:23:44.680
He... Harald brought the
"outside" into the "inside."

00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:49.320
That would be our assumption in this matter.

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:58.060
As a result, the "boundary" is wavering greatly.

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:03.660
Can you explain that in smaller bites?

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:11.680
Y- You're doing that
on purpose, aren't you?

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:16.410
Every kind of society places the world
in order by the concept of opposites:

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:19.510
Inside and outside, religious
and secular, celestial and worldly.

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:23.220
Those opposing concepts
organize the world as it is today.

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:31.060
But none of those can be distinctly separated.

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:35.760
There is always a gray area
where it is ambiguous.

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:44.710
Tomonari Kasumi, a.k.a. Sieg,
who went into a coma in Kanazawa...

00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:47.140
...was inside the game.

00:24:47.210 --> 00:24:50.910
However, Kasumi himself is clearly
an existence outside the game.

00:24:55.190 --> 00:24:59.820
Then, which side was his consciousness in?

00:24:59.890 --> 00:25:02.020
The inside, or the outside?

00:25:04.330 --> 00:25:09.830
Do you get it? It's possible
to explain it either way.

00:25:09.900 --> 00:25:14.170
Yeah. Reason and plaster can stick to anything.

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:16.770
That's right.

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:19.800
However, to make them stick
without forcing them together...

00:25:19.880 --> 00:25:22.870
...you must control it to an extent.

00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:25.820
Then, we give it a meaning.

00:25:25.890 --> 00:25:32.550
In anthropology, that is called
nature of boundaries, or "liminality."

00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:36.160
Liminality?

00:25:36.230 --> 00:25:38.420
It's a bit different, but may I?

00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:40.190
Uh, sure.

00:25:40.270 --> 00:25:43.500
When my family moved
here from Suginami...

00:25:43.570 --> 00:25:47.800
...we were the "outsiders"
that came to the "inside" of Hida.

00:25:47.870 --> 00:25:52.310
My parents chose to assimilate themselves
to the "inside" by working at it for two years.

00:25:54.550 --> 00:25:58.250
But I am still on the "outside."

00:25:59.450 --> 00:26:02.250
So, your boundaries are wavering as well.

00:26:03.320 --> 00:26:08.120
But this isn't where I belong.

00:26:09.260 --> 00:26:11.360
So the answer is as simple as that.

00:26:12.470 --> 00:26:14.230
What do you mean?

00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:17.960
You just separate the "outside"
and the "inside." Right?

00:26:24.880 --> 00:26:29.280
Just like you, who will grow up
and leave this city...

00:26:29.350 --> 00:26:34.310
...fortunately the "outside" that Harald
brought inside the game...

00:26:34.390 --> 00:26:37.220
...also seems to be autonomous.

00:26:37.290 --> 00:26:40.350
If so, all we have to do is help it.

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.250
How?

00:26:43.330 --> 00:26:47.600
From this point on, it will
require determination on your part.

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:51.300
After all, in the worst-case scenario,
we will all become criminals.

00:26:53.010 --> 00:26:54.970
Do you still want to listen?

00:27:17.030 --> 00:27:18.330
Please tell us.

00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:32.810
What if I asked you to pretend
we never had that conversation?

00:27:34.350 --> 00:27:36.940
We will lose our means of opposition...

00:27:37.020 --> 00:27:41.280
...and CC Corp. will destroy the server
in order to bury everything into darkness.

00:27:41.350 --> 00:27:42.690
You're kidding...

00:27:42.760 --> 00:27:45.130
That's what CC Corp. intends to do.

00:27:45.130 --> 00:27:49.360
If that happens, the clues to save
the comatose victims will be lost forever.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:59.630
Well, I'll see you on
Christmas Eve in Urayasu.

00:28:04.110 --> 00:28:06.080
This is getting totally out of hand.

00:28:07.050 --> 00:28:10.680
Even if the worst case scenario
doesn't happen, it's still a crime.

00:28:12.390 --> 00:28:14.180
Still wanna do it?

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:26.730
Yeah. This is my game.

00:28:32.510 --> 00:28:37.110
Tasogare no umi ni dete...
<i>Setting out in twilight seas...</i>

00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:42.010
Futari wa nidoto mou meguri...
<i>Will we never meet...</i>

00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:46.920
...aenaino?
<i>... again?</i>

00:28:53.760 --> 00:29:00.930
Kin no akari ga umi ni ochite...
<i>A light of gold falls into the sea...</i>

00:29:01.430 --> 00:29:06.460
...natsu no kaze ga togireta.
<i>... the wind of summer trails off.</i>

00:29:06.840 --> 00:29:12.040
Obieru futari ni tada...
<i>The frightened pair only hears the sound...</i>

00:29:12.110 --> 00:29:17.950
...yosetekaesu mizuoto.
<i>... of sea water coming and going again.</i>

00:29:19.790 --> 00:29:25.050
Donnani nami wo kasanete...
<i>No matter how I drown the waves...</i>

00:29:25.130 --> 00:29:30.430
Omoide wo sakendemo...
<i>Screaming out our memories...</i>

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:35.730
Anata no ita kishibe niwa...
<i>I can never return to the shore...</i>

00:29:35.800 --> 00:29:41.210
...mou kaerenai.
<i>... where you were.</i>

00:29:41.810 --> 00:29:46.440
Tasogare dake wo daite.
<i>Embrace nothing but the twilight sky.</i>

00:29:46.510 --> 00:29:49.710
Ano hi no nami wa mou...
<i>The waves from that day are now...</i>

00:29:49.780 --> 00:29:53.410
...fukai umi no soko.
<i>... at the bottom of the deep ocean.</i>

00:29:53.490 --> 00:29:57.080
Kanashimi wo shiranai...
<i>They sleep as they embrace blue dreams...</i>

00:29:57.160 --> 00:30:02.090
...aoi yume wo mite nemutteiru.
<i>... that do not know sorrow.</i>
